WEBVTT

00:05.630 --> 00:08.800
It's so high up! But it feels kind of nice, too!

00:08.880 --> 00:11.840
We pulled an all-nighter
putting it together. Don't break it...

00:13.680 --> 00:17.350
--This is great!
--Don't let go! Sheesh...!

00:17.430 --> 00:20.180
So, what are "regulations"?

00:20.810 --> 00:25.140
They're meant to ensure
machines meet the standards for racing.

00:25.230 --> 00:28.480
It makes a race pointless
if the machines are too different.

00:28.570 --> 00:30.440
And the Fuego's no good?

00:30.530 --> 00:33.700
Yeah. The Fuego looks like a market model,

00:33.780 --> 00:37.370
but Okakura made a lot of
customizations on the inside.

00:37.450 --> 00:41.450
Even the frame breaks regulation,
so we can't enter it in races.

00:41.540 --> 00:43.080
Oh...

00:43.160 --> 00:44.000
Don't worry.

00:44.080 --> 00:47.580
The Balon is a new
Teryan Kaduro model, just like the Fuego.

00:47.670 --> 00:50.460
It has the same control type, so I'm sure you'll--

00:58.890 --> 00:59.800
That was close!

00:59.890 --> 01:02.970
Aww, man! I told you to be careful!

01:03.060 --> 01:04.680
I'm sorry!

01:04.770 --> 01:08.230
That's enough!
Stop playing around and lend us a hand!

01:08.310 --> 01:09.690
Yes, Ma'am...

01:14.530 --> 01:16.400
Feel uneasy without the Fuego?

01:18.070 --> 01:19.120
What's this?

01:19.200 --> 01:21.580
Your reward for practicing hard.

01:22.450 --> 01:26.120
You've done well these past few weeks of training.

01:26.210 --> 01:28.250
You should be more than ready to race now.

01:29.500 --> 01:31.250
Thank you.

01:31.340 --> 01:34.840
We face off tomorrow.
I'm going to settle things this time.

01:35.720 --> 01:37.630
Colonel Romanov Cullenberg,
the soon-to-be commander

01:37.720 --> 01:42.560
of the GGP's Security Enforcement
Unit, arrived at the Yokota Air Base.

01:42.640 --> 01:44.560
Present at his inaugural ceremony next week

01:44.640 --> 01:47.980
will be the prime minister
and cabinet ministers, as well as--

03:31.000 --> 03:32.420
An RBZ!

03:33.790 --> 03:37.550
Nice! That's the last in the flagship
line of entirely-Japanese models!

03:37.630 --> 03:39.590
I'm amazed she got one!

03:40.300 --> 03:42.550
Kataoka's gonna win again this year!

03:46.810 --> 03:49.390
--Outta the way!
--Dumbass!

03:49.470 --> 03:51.600
Get your slow ass off the track!

03:54.440 --> 03:56.940
Mr. Okakura. The course
marshal briefing is about to begin.

03:57.020 --> 03:58.230
Yeah.

04:06.330 --> 04:12.040
This is the Kanto Circuit's live
"Excitement Pit in Out" FM radio show!

04:12.120 --> 04:14.120
I'm DJ Yuji, and with me is Mr. Ride.

04:14.210 --> 04:20.130
We'll be commentating
this RideBack national championship...

04:20.210 --> 04:22.720
Shoko! Over here!

04:23.510 --> 04:25.760
I brought some gifts!

04:25.840 --> 04:27.800
Oh, that looks good!

04:27.890 --> 04:29.810
Thanks for coming all the way out here!

04:29.890 --> 04:32.140
I had nothing else to do, so...

04:32.230 --> 04:34.480
This is nice, it's almost like a festival!

04:34.560 --> 04:38.520
It only takes place once a year,
so they have to make it exciting.

04:38.610 --> 04:40.980
For some teams, this is like a party.

04:41.070 --> 04:45.450
But not for us, though.
We're the defending champions.

04:45.530 --> 04:48.240
--Where's Rin?
--She's test-driving with Tamayo.

04:48.330 --> 04:49.740
Oh, they're back!

05:03.550 --> 05:06.760
All right, what kind of driving was that?!

05:06.840 --> 05:08.970
It wouldn't turn how I wanted...

05:09.050 --> 05:12.470
It sort of felt like the handles were pulling me...

05:12.560 --> 05:14.520
It's hard to explain...

05:15.390 --> 05:19.150
Hishida. Try increasing the Balon's LSD control level.

05:19.230 --> 05:21.440
And take another look
at the absorber resistance levels,

05:21.530 --> 05:23.730
it needs to go deeper into its left turns.

05:23.820 --> 05:27.610
What?! The qualifiers are in two hours!
That's barely enough time--

05:27.700 --> 05:30.070
This won't be much of a race otherwise.

05:34.540 --> 05:37.330
The handles are pulling, huh...

05:37.420 --> 05:40.790
Do you think you can win a second time in a row?!

05:40.880 --> 05:42.460
That is why I'm here.

05:42.550 --> 05:44.800
Is your father cheering for you too?

05:44.880 --> 05:46.550
My father has nothing to do with this.

05:47.590 --> 05:51.180
Is Tamayo's father famous or something?

05:51.260 --> 05:55.060
He's Nanpu Kataoka, a big shot
in the ruling party's largest faction.

05:55.140 --> 05:58.230
He's even served as the finance
and foreign minister in the past!

05:58.310 --> 05:59.940
Haven't you seen him on TV?

06:00.020 --> 06:02.310
Oh, that really evil-looking guy?!

06:02.400 --> 06:03.190
You idiot!

06:03.230 --> 06:06.530
On top of that, her brother
is a big-shot police official.

06:07.200 --> 06:12.530
Mr. Kataoka. I take it you've met the
new commander during GGP training?

06:12.620 --> 06:15.660
Yes. He was a special instructor or something.

06:17.120 --> 06:20.790
I hear he gained prominence
leading a RideBack squad.

06:20.880 --> 06:23.790
The Arizona Campaign was the legendary battle

06:23.880 --> 06:27.420
that supposedly changed
the tide of war for the struggling GGP.

06:27.510 --> 06:30.090
But there isn't a single official record of it.

06:30.180 --> 06:33.100
It's one of the big mysteries of the GGP.

06:33.810 --> 06:35.770
Smells suspicious...

06:36.640 --> 06:39.640
Mr. Kataoka. This way, please.

06:39.730 --> 06:42.480
I guess it's time to greet this odorous commander.

06:43.320 --> 06:46.860
The qualifying race to determine
the starting grid order is underway!

06:46.940 --> 06:50.990
The key is not to fall behind
in the off-road mountain area!

06:51.070 --> 06:55.530
<i>It isn't a setting issue. Was she</i>
<i>faster before because of the Fuego?</i>

06:56.790 --> 06:58.660
Oh, here she comes!

06:58.750 --> 07:00.750
--You can do it, Rin!
--Rin!

07:00.830 --> 07:03.040
No good! Her time isn't coming down!

07:03.130 --> 07:05.420
It's like she's barely able to drive out there...

07:05.500 --> 07:07.090
Like you're one to talk...

07:08.630 --> 07:09.880
Rin...

07:09.970 --> 07:13.760
It's her first race, so just
finishing the race would be a great feat.

07:13.850 --> 07:17.560
Besides, a complete novice
entering this race is crazy to begin with.

07:17.640 --> 07:21.310
I thought Rin would be fast in any machine,

07:21.390 --> 07:23.810
but I guess RideBacks have
different chemistry with different people.

07:23.900 --> 07:27.780
They don't. They're all the same
when they're on the same settings.

07:28.610 --> 07:32.280
But the Fuego does have its own peculiarities.

07:32.360 --> 07:34.410
In that sense, you could call it different chemistry.

07:34.490 --> 07:37.450
Come on, now. You know that's nonsense.

07:37.540 --> 07:39.700
I'd been wondering about it for a while.

07:39.790 --> 07:43.420
Tamayo hated the Fuego,
saying it was hard to control.

07:43.500 --> 07:46.540
But Rin drove it like a charm.
Doesn't that seem strange?

07:46.630 --> 07:47.800
That's true...

07:49.050 --> 07:51.970
<i>This isn't going well... Something's hampering me...</i>

07:52.050 --> 07:53.300
<i>What could it be?</i>

07:53.390 --> 07:55.260
<i>If I was in the Fuego...</i>

07:59.850 --> 08:03.520
Damn it! Stop playing around, asshole!

08:10.690 --> 08:12.320
We'll get you for this!

08:12.900 --> 08:15.360
Payback for messing with my girl!

08:22.830 --> 08:27.960
The defending champ, Tamayo Kataoka,
is already tearing up the course!

08:28.040 --> 08:30.130
Oh! She came in first in the qualifiers!

08:30.210 --> 08:32.170
--Wow!
--All right!

08:33.510 --> 08:36.840
The Fuego's ACS settings...

08:36.930 --> 08:41.430
Its matrix is really fragmented.
Almost like it's useless...

08:41.520 --> 08:44.810
Why would Okakura use these settings?

08:47.440 --> 08:51.400
Hishida! What are you tinkering with mine for?!

08:51.480 --> 08:53.860
Reset my cuff fork settings.

08:53.950 --> 08:56.820
And third-gear is slow to
accelerate, so swap in a new gear.

08:56.910 --> 09:00.370
We won't have time to test it, though!
You just came in first, too...

09:00.450 --> 09:02.410
It's no big deal.

09:02.500 --> 09:04.870
Also, about the Balon's settings...

09:04.960 --> 09:08.330
A-About that... It's a little reckless, but...

09:10.090 --> 09:12.460
Sink or swim, huh?

09:12.550 --> 09:14.220
Okay, give it a shot!

09:14.300 --> 09:15.340
Right!

09:21.720 --> 09:22.930
Good job, Rin!

09:23.020 --> 09:25.060
You came in 17th!

09:26.140 --> 09:27.230
Thanks.

09:29.480 --> 09:31.860
Hishida! Ten minutes until the race!

09:31.940 --> 09:34.820
This should about do it!

09:37.740 --> 09:42.080
Is Rin going to be okay?
She looks really down in the dumps...

09:42.160 --> 09:44.120
She always looks that way before a performance.

09:44.200 --> 09:45.160
Huh?

09:45.250 --> 09:47.210
That's how she concentrates.

09:47.290 --> 09:50.710
Rin would never give up
easily, no matter the situation.

09:50.790 --> 09:52.880
I can just tell.

09:52.960 --> 09:56.760
At last, it's time for the All-Japan
RideBack championship race to begin!

09:56.840 --> 09:59.430
I'm your announcer,
Go Kurumada, of the CS Motor Channel.

09:59.510 --> 10:03.850
With me for commentary is
Chief Editor Suzuki of RideBack Magazine.

10:03.930 --> 10:07.100
Hello! This is Suzuki!

10:07.190 --> 10:09.100
Well, the qualifying race ended with--

10:09.190 --> 10:12.230
Simply put, I removed the Balon's ACS,

10:12.320 --> 10:16.690
the device that provides riding assistance.

10:17.740 --> 10:19.200
ACS?

10:19.280 --> 10:22.530
The Fuego has one too, of course,
but when I checked its backup data

10:22.620 --> 10:26.120
I saw that its settings
had made it essentially useless.

10:26.200 --> 10:31.210
So I tried removing the Balon's ACS
to make it more like the Fuego.

10:34.500 --> 10:37.510
Remember to take it nice and slow at the start.

10:37.590 --> 10:39.340
--Good luck out there!
--Right!

10:39.430 --> 10:42.640
The RideBack championship race is about to begin!

10:42.720 --> 10:46.720
Will last year's champion,
Tamayo Kataoka, achieve a second win in a row?!

10:46.810 --> 10:49.390
Can the team that came in behind her, the Cobras,

10:49.480 --> 10:51.810
dispel last year's humiliation
with victory wine this year?!

10:51.900 --> 10:54.980
--My heart is throbbing!
--Rin! Good luck!

10:55.070 --> 10:58.530
Don't you think it's
dangerous for her to race like that?

10:58.610 --> 11:01.160
Yeah, it's definitely sink or swim.

11:01.240 --> 11:05.280
But I get the feeling that
Rin can handle it just fine.

11:05.370 --> 11:09.750
We're just seconds away from the start of the race!

11:35.520 --> 11:37.610
Damn! We didn't get her!

11:38.280 --> 11:39.900
You guys are way too obvious!

11:39.990 --> 11:42.610
All right! Kataoka's through the first corner!

11:42.700 --> 11:43.740
What about Rin?!

11:45.330 --> 11:47.580
Yikes! She started too late!

11:47.660 --> 11:54.670
Benjamin Franklin, in Paris
to enlist continuing French support

11:54.750 --> 11:57.800
--for the American Revolution, joined the crowd...

11:57.800 --> 11:59.420
--Nice start!
--for the American Revolution, joined the crowd...

11:59.510 --> 12:01.510
Ogata! Translate, please!

12:01.590 --> 12:04.590
R-Right! U-Umm...

12:04.680 --> 12:06.640
I don't know.

12:12.310 --> 12:15.770
It's been a long time. Welcome to Japan.

12:19.820 --> 12:23.900
The lead group passes the main stands,
with Kataoka in the pole position!

12:23.990 --> 12:26.780
She's followed by Takeshi, the older Cobra brother,

12:26.870 --> 12:28.580
and Hiroshi, the younger brother.

12:28.660 --> 12:30.790
There are currently 22 machines on the track.

12:30.870 --> 12:35.170
None have dropped out yet, but
the winner will clearly be one of these three.

12:35.250 --> 12:37.840
The RBZ is still in first.

12:37.920 --> 12:41.130
--What about the Balon?
--Umm... second to last.

12:42.090 --> 12:44.720
--Is she going to be all right?
--You can do it, Rin!

12:45.510 --> 12:47.010
Oh, she moved up!

12:47.100 --> 12:49.640
The off-road mountain course shows all green.

12:49.720 --> 12:53.100
Lead rider #710 is entering the mountain course.

12:55.810 --> 12:57.770
Rin moved up again!

12:57.860 --> 12:59.820
She just might do this!

13:01.150 --> 13:05.530
<i>It swings wide in the corners,</i>
<i>but it's moving exactly how I want now...</i>

13:07.030 --> 13:11.120
Are you against the introduction
of police RideBacks as well?

13:11.200 --> 13:13.660
My opinion is of no concern.

13:13.750 --> 13:17.420
We simply wish to expend all
measures to verify their viability

13:17.500 --> 13:19.670
before commencing with their introduction.

13:19.750 --> 13:22.250
What pretentious opposition.

13:22.340 --> 13:24.170
I'm here to clean up after my predecessor,

13:24.260 --> 13:27.550
who couldn't get anything
done because of you people.

13:27.640 --> 13:29.680
Don't expect any mercy.

13:29.760 --> 13:32.470
My country dissolved its RideBack squad

13:32.560 --> 13:35.430
because localized skirmishes became unnecessary.

13:35.520 --> 13:37.600
But it's different in this country.

13:37.690 --> 13:39.520
RideBacks have already been used

13:39.610 --> 13:41.770
in terrorist attacks in Sasebo and Kokura.

13:41.860 --> 13:45.240
In short, they're rather effective
weapons in this small country of yours.

13:46.280 --> 13:48.910
We can deal with them with our current equipment.

13:48.990 --> 13:50.910
Do you want to turn your country into a place

13:50.990 --> 13:54.040
where armored cars on the streets are the norm?

13:54.120 --> 13:55.580
That isn't my point.

13:55.660 --> 13:59.580
I'm simply saying that we don't
believe that motorcycles with arms

13:59.670 --> 14:01.920
would be an effective method of deterrence.

14:03.130 --> 14:07.720
You Japanese really are
an aggravatingly uptight people.

14:07.800 --> 14:10.470
We had one in our squad, in fact.

14:10.550 --> 14:15.180
Though, in his case, he actually
became a hero by riding a RideBack.

14:15.270 --> 14:18.140
The race enters the off-road track,
with Tamayo Kataoka still in the lead

14:18.230 --> 14:20.730
and the Cobra brothers chasing close behind!

14:20.810 --> 14:23.860
Damn you, Kataoka! I refuse to let you win!

14:23.940 --> 14:25.730
You don't know when to give up!

14:26.780 --> 14:31.280
One rider, #711, has broken out
of the rear and passed six other riders!

14:31.370 --> 14:34.410
A strong showing for her
very first competition appearance!

14:34.490 --> 14:36.870
Man, that's dangerous riding!

14:44.500 --> 14:46.260
That riding style...

14:47.340 --> 14:49.720
Wow! She passed another one!

14:49.800 --> 14:51.260
Way to go, Rin!

14:51.340 --> 14:54.140
Huh? Okakura? Isn't he a race marshal?

14:54.220 --> 14:55.310
Hello?

14:55.390 --> 14:57.850
You undid the Balon's ACS, didn't you?

14:59.190 --> 15:02.940
You found out?
It isn't against regulations, though.

15:03.020 --> 15:05.320
It's a problem to the other machines.

15:05.400 --> 15:07.280
Get her into the pit and drop out of the race.

15:07.360 --> 15:10.110
Huh? But she is climbing up the ranks...

15:10.200 --> 15:11.450
You're saying it's not a problem?!

15:11.530 --> 15:15.530
Okay, I understand. I'll signal her into the pit--

15:15.620 --> 15:16.580
Oh!

15:16.660 --> 15:17.700
What's wrong?!

15:17.790 --> 15:20.710
I haven't taught her how to read signboards...

15:21.920 --> 15:23.790
Do something, you idiot!

15:23.880 --> 15:25.670
Is something wrong?

15:25.750 --> 15:29.590
Okakura wants her to drop out of
the race because the Balon is dangerous.

15:29.670 --> 15:30.970
How come?!

15:31.050 --> 15:34.260
He found out I turned off the Balon's ACS.

15:34.350 --> 15:36.260
What's an ACS--

15:36.350 --> 15:40.600
A device that automatically corrects
the suspension's control balance.

15:40.690 --> 15:43.940
RideBacks are really unstable without them,

15:41.330 --> 15:47.340
Rin - come back to the pit!

15:44.020 --> 15:47.610
so even the tiniest bumps in
the road will knock 'em over.

15:47.690 --> 15:50.650
Rin's in serious danger then!

15:50.740 --> 15:55.620
Normally, yes. But Rin's riding
faster now than she did in the qualifiers.

15:55.700 --> 16:00.330
It's just a guess, but I think her
reflexes are faster than the auto-correction

16:00.410 --> 16:03.620
and that she's making different,
instantaneous corrections on her own.

16:05.130 --> 16:08.170
It's hard to believe, but Rin is riding.

16:08.250 --> 16:10.130
What's this? Someone's
breaking ahead of the rear pack!

16:10.210 --> 16:12.220
It's Ms. Kataoka's junior...

16:12.300 --> 16:13.340
<i>I've figured it out!</i>

16:13.430 --> 16:17.050
She's catching up quickly!
Her lap time isn't half-bad, either!

16:17.140 --> 16:18.930
She's caught up with the middle pack!

16:19.020 --> 16:23.940
#711 is catching up fast! She passed
three middle-packriders in one shot!

16:24.020 --> 16:25.900
--One more and she'll be a prizewinner!

16:25.900 --> 16:26.810
--Go!
--One more and she'll be a prizewinner!

16:26.900 --> 16:27.940
Rin...

16:29.440 --> 16:31.070
#711 closes in!

16:31.150 --> 16:37.120
Wow! This rookie's time in Sector 3
was faster than everyone in the lead!

16:37.200 --> 16:41.330
<i>Whoa, this sounds exciting! I-I wanna watch...</i>

16:42.960 --> 16:45.540
Looks like she's finally hit her stride.

16:47.960 --> 16:50.670
Win, Big Bro!

16:53.340 --> 16:55.510
Hiroshi! Your death won't be in vain--

16:55.590 --> 16:57.970
So it's a fight, huh?! You're going down!

16:58.050 --> 16:59.010
Shit!

17:01.100 --> 17:03.350
Those snake brothers are just terrible!

17:03.430 --> 17:04.810
Should we complain?

17:04.890 --> 17:08.270
No, Okakura's a marshal so he's probably watching.

17:08.360 --> 17:10.270
If anything, you should try to keep Kataoka

17:10.360 --> 17:12.480
from killing those two after the race.

17:13.570 --> 17:18.450
...the homestretch with the older
Cobra in the lead by only a thin margin!

17:22.250 --> 17:23.700
<i>I caught up!</i>

17:25.250 --> 17:27.000
It's about time.

17:31.670 --> 17:34.170
--Sir, about this subjunctive...
--Hmm? Which one?

17:34.260 --> 17:35.840
Just a peek...

17:35.930 --> 17:39.390
--not Ms. Kataoka, but rather her junior!

17:39.470 --> 17:44.220
There's no question about it!
#711 is a new RideBack princess!

17:44.310 --> 17:46.810
Her name is--

17:46.890 --> 17:50.860
Ready to face the consequences, Ogata?

17:50.940 --> 17:52.820
Y-Yes...

17:54.900 --> 17:58.490
--Rin's in fourth place!
--She always has me in suspense!

17:59.990 --> 18:01.160
<i>Just a little more...</i>

18:03.160 --> 18:06.750
<i>But there's definitely something</i>
<i>different about it than the Fuego...</i>

18:08.500 --> 18:09.730
Rin - come back to the pit!

18:09.960 --> 18:12.210
Are you sure we shouldn't use this?

18:12.300 --> 18:15.420
It is the final lap and all...

18:15.510 --> 18:17.090
It's Okakura, isn't it?

18:18.550 --> 18:19.890
I guess she's okay after all--

18:19.970 --> 18:22.850
Are you listening to the Balon's exhaust note?

18:22.930 --> 18:26.100
The engine's burning.
I'm holding you responsible for the costs.

18:26.180 --> 18:27.140
Oh no!

18:27.770 --> 18:32.110
Oh, my! What's happened to #711, Ms. Ogata?!

18:32.190 --> 18:34.480
The engine's toast.

18:34.570 --> 18:35.480
What a shame!

18:35.570 --> 18:40.360
After a brilliant come-from-behind run,
Ms. Ogata has slid off the course!

18:40.450 --> 18:42.410
She's out of the race!

18:45.750 --> 18:50.210
Does this mean the Balon
couldn't keep up with her riding...?

18:50.290 --> 18:53.080
The older Cobra brother
takes the lead in the last corner!

18:53.170 --> 18:56.760
<i>Rin. Our match is on hold until next year.</i>

19:11.940 --> 19:13.860
I'm sorry...

19:24.410 --> 19:31.580
We have no records of a Japanese
man in the GGP's RideBack squad...

19:31.670 --> 19:34.540
No. Not even rumors of it.

19:36.710 --> 19:39.670
But I can guess who it might be.

19:39.760 --> 19:43.300
A peculiar returnee that
Public Security is secretly monitoring

19:43.390 --> 19:45.850
at the request of the GGP.

19:45.930 --> 19:48.720
What's more, I'm told RideBacks are his hobby.

19:52.020 --> 19:54.440
Cheers!

19:56.360 --> 20:01.070
You gave those snake brothers a real walloping...

20:01.150 --> 20:03.950
You're amazing, Tamayo...!

20:04.030 --> 20:06.580
I was deeply moved!

20:06.660 --> 20:08.620
All right, who let her drink?!

20:08.700 --> 20:13.420
She's still underage,
so all she's had is orange juice.

20:13.500 --> 20:18.000
Rin would've won fourth place
if the Balon hadn't broke down...

20:18.090 --> 20:19.420
Stupid Balon!

20:19.510 --> 20:22.340
Was the smell enough to get her drunk?!

20:22.430 --> 20:24.130
Huh? Where is she, anyway?

20:24.220 --> 20:27.180
Oh, Rin? She went out for a walk on the Fuego.

20:49.950 --> 20:51.660
What's the matter?

20:51.750 --> 20:55.290
I'm sorry about the Balon...

20:56.960 --> 21:00.420
That was an engineering mistake.
It wasn't any fault of yours.

21:01.920 --> 21:03.720
Can I ask you something?

21:03.800 --> 21:06.300
When you were first in the Fuego,

21:06.390 --> 21:09.780
why did you decide to jump instead of stop?

21:10.510 --> 21:13.060
I was so flustered that I don't really know.

21:13.140 --> 21:17.230
I just felt like I could trust
the Fuego, for some reason.

21:18.770 --> 21:21.650
I'm going to ride for a little bit longer.

21:56.730 --> 22:01.310
Even when he laughs

22:03.400 --> 22:08.950
I'm thinking of you before I realize it

22:12.030 --> 22:16.910
And the hands holding his

22:18.830 --> 22:24.250
feel your warmth, too

22:26.470 --> 22:30.220
Even if I cut out my recollections

22:30.300 --> 22:34.180
and drive them out of my heart

22:34.270 --> 22:37.930
or try to kick the memories out

22:38.020 --> 22:42.400
I still think of you

22:42.480 --> 22:46.900
Time now passes and seasons fly by

22:46.990 --> 22:50.740
Even if that smile starts to become hazy

22:50.820 --> 22:54.740
my heart will never forget you

22:54.830 --> 22:58.500
(even if we can never meet again)

22:58.580 --> 23:02.330
Even if I knock over photos of us smiling

23:02.420 --> 23:06.630
or try to hide my overflowing feelings

23:07.720 --> 23:10.880
my heart will never forget

23:11.680 --> 23:14.930
my memories with you

23:26.030 --> 23:41.020
New Hishida Theatre

23:27.320 --> 23:30.860
Okakura. About the Balon's repairs...

23:30.950 --> 23:35.790
Engine overhauls are really expensive...
Could you increase our budget?

23:35.870 --> 23:39.560
Next Episode:

23:35.870 --> 23:39.560
A Close Call for Shoko

23:37.500 --> 23:40.540
You were sleeping?!
Your facial expressions are too unclear!
